# A bool inside a container. The element tag vocabulary that tells a list's element from text or
# a float has no bool in it, so both backends print the number a bool is stored as: `[1, 1]` and
# `{'k': 1}` where CPython prints `[True, 1]` and `{'k': True}` (roadmap Gap R.112, filed by ADR
# 0257 — the print rule landed there; the element tag of the ADR 0184 vocabulary still has to grow).
print([True, 1])
print({"k": True})
